title Caravan commute -- a shared region is a hazard only where someone may write it
prompt Kyri voice and Radiant first, then REMEMBER, the itineraries, and the newest log recommends; close open agent-closable reds Standfast-first, then take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; send each finished increment as its own signed round
think Standfast first -- read crux/REDS.md whole. Rows 81 through 87 all read closed and released, including the 20260819.134229 reopen-and-close of 85 and the 20260819.145920 close of 84. No open agent-closable red stands, so the constructive queue is honestly open.
think The running thread came from the newest log's recommend line, and it named the crux exactly: the order test reads which regions an item names and nothing about what the item does to them, so a reader and a writer of one region read as equally ordered when only one direction is real.
think Reading overtake.rye's share_a_hop and rolling.admissible together showed the question is bigger than the recommend framed it. Both tests reduce to relay.share_a_region or a region-name comparison, so BOTH rooms -- the instant and the order -- count a shared read as a conflict. One refinement answers both, and the source is the same: the grant's own permission word.
think Nothing new needs declaring, which is overtake's own lesson one turn on. Every declaration this arc reads already writes rw or r beside each grant, and regions.Map already answers may_write by name. So the whole of the new knowledge is one call into a map the document already built.
think The elder three-client shape has no region two clients share, so it could not measure the finding. serial_three_clients_menu.bron adds the one thing an ordinary server has that the shape never carried -- a menu published once by the virtualiser and read by all three clients -- and adds no new kind of word to say it. Ten regions, nineteen grants, everything else unmoved.
think The supervised child path had no word for read and change nothing: place, pass, and home each write before they finish, and gap.attempt refused peek outright. Accreted peek to gap.attempt, delegating to a do_peek that mirrors cycle.rye's exactly, so one word keeps one spelling. The three verbs a ring under fall asks are untouched, and gap plus decline re-ran GREEN after.
think Three readings over one program: by_region carried unchanged from overtake, by_grant the refinement, reads_free the control that wants both sides writing before it orders anything -- which reads the write-then-read arc as commuting and is exactly the mistake worth proving.
obs The finding has two halves and they separate cleanly. Over the reading lap direction converts the whole of it -- 6 slot-turns unspent by region against 0 by grant, a peak of 1 against 3, 2 lawful passes reaching 2 items back, 4 children to the same end. Over the published lap, whose head writes what the readers hold, the ORDER half converts nothing (0 passes under both) while the ISOLATION half still converts 2 slot-turns of 6. One refinement, two rooms, and the write closes exactly one of them.
obs Read straight, the pair count says it in one number: 0 pairs of these four domains may hold the machine at once by region, 3 by grant. A read counted as a hazard collapses the widest set from three to one.
obs Reuse over restatement held throughout -- relay.share_a_region, overtake.share_a_hop, rolling.admissible, cohort.spawn_one and reap_one, and overtake.Report all asked rather than restated, so the two rungs' numbers stand side by side unconverted. The supervisor loop is overtake's program differing in two calls.
obs Both RED paths proven on metal before any GREEN claim. Run the reading lap by region under the fine reading's own checks and it reds at 6 slot-turns unspent, so the conversion is real work. Run the published lap under reads_free and 2 items pass a head that writes what they read, so its zero passes is a refusal earned rather than an absence of candidates.
obs The control breaks where the document said it would: 1 pass taken, the home hears no bell that was never rung, OutcomeMismatch. Faster and wrong, measured rather than argued.
obs Council rota lap 469 mod 27 = 10 -- sameness-is-the-macro, read deep. It shaped the round directly: the compression here came from asking the existing declarations one question further rather than growing a private dialect for direction, and every reused predicate is a line saved that stays free forever.
loom witness=caravan_commute_witness reading_lap_slots_by_region=6 reading_lap_slots_by_grant=0 peak_by_region=1 peak_by_grant=3 lawful_passes=2 pass_reach=2 published_passes=0 published_slots_converted=2 free_pairs_by_region=0 free_pairs_by_grant=3 control_passes=1 children=4
file caravan/commute.rye the rung -- direction read from the grants, applied in both rooms, three readings over one program
file caravan/systems/serial_three_clients_menu.bron the elder three-client shape plus one published region every client reads and only the virtualiser writes
file tools/caravan_commute_witness.rish the witness, GREEN on metal, both RED paths named
file caravan/gap.rye one word accreted to attempt -- peek, which reads an index and changes nothing
file caravan/README.md the roster row and the Commute section, docs synced in the same commit as the code
recommend keep-going the honest next crux is what direction still cannot see -- the grant is an upper bound rather than an act, so a domain holding rw on a region it only reads this turn still orders every reader behind it, and the question becomes whether an item may declare the direction of its own hop without letting a supervisor take an item at its word
